W44-116 per-step XYB dump in buttloop's recon pipeline
=======================================================

Date: 2026-05-20
Branch: (sibling workspace) jxl-encoder--w44-116-recon-step-dump
Parent commit: 3882e14a (main, W44-113 audit memo)
Run on: water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, archmage X64V3 SIMD

Command (per-mode invocation; all 4 modes concatenated into TSV):

  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
    cargo run --release --example w44_116_per_step_dump \
    --features '__internal_recon_hook butteraugli-loop' \
    --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml

Modes (env-gated):
  1. gab ON  + EPF ON    (default; rows 2-25)
  2. gab OFF + EPF ON    (W44_116_NO_GAB=1; rows 26-49)
  3. gab ON  + EPF OFF   (W44_116_NO_EPF=1; rows 50-73)
  4. gab OFF + EPF OFF   (both env vars; rows 74-97)

Cells (4 × 4 modes = 16 encode runs, 6 step rows each = 96 data rows):
  1025469 d=2 e8 (CID22 photo, 512×512)
  1025469 d=4 e8
  terminal d=2 e8  (gb82-sc screenshot, 1646×1062)
  terminal d=4 e8

Columns:
  image, distance, effort, width, height, gab (label "on"/"off"),
  step (after_recon_xyb / after_gab / after_epf / after_patches /
        after_splines / anchor_internal_recon),
  step_ran (1 if step executed, 0 if skipped — NaN values follow),
  maxabs_r/g/b: per-channel max-absolute delta vs jxl-rs decoded
                linear-RGB (clamp to [0,1] both sides),
  meanabs_r/g/b: same but mean,
  delta_vs_prev_maxabs_r/g/b: step's maxabs MINUS previous step's
                              maxabs (negative = step brought us
                              CLOSER to jxl-rs; positive = step
                              made things WORSE),
  bytes: bitstream size.

The "anchor_internal_recon" row is the existing W44-111 InternalRecon
hook output (post-pipeline cropped linear-RGB) for cross-validation
that the per-step dump matches the established baseline. It must
match the last "ran=1" step within FP noise.

Headline findings (see W44-116 memo for full discussion):

Mode 4 (gab OFF + EPF OFF), 1025469 cells:
  after_recon_xyb max-abs = 0.000004 / 0.000002 / 0.000002 (FP noise).
  → reconstruct_xyb IS AT PARITY with jxl-rs's recon path.

Mode 3 (gab ON + EPF OFF), 1025469 cells:
  after_recon_xyb max-abs = 0.50 R (gab not yet applied),
  after_gab max-abs = 0.000004 R (FP noise).
  → gab_smooth IS AT PARITY with jxl-rs's GaborishStage.

Mode 2 (gab OFF + EPF ON), 1025469 cells:
  after_recon_xyb max-abs = 0.047 R,
  after_epf max-abs = 0.047 R (EPF barely moves the delta).
  → bitstream differs (different buttloop convergence with EPF on),
    EPF in our pipeline matches jxl-rs's, but the buttloop's
    INTERNAL EPF used uniform sharpness=4 while the bitstream
    encodes the production sharpness map.

Mode 1 (gab ON + EPF ON), 1025469 cells:
  after_recon_xyb max-abs = 0.51 R, after_gab = 0.067 R,
  after_epf = 0.061 R, anchor = 0.061 R.
  → matches W44-111 baseline (R = 0.0608 ± 0.001 on 1025469 d=2 e8).

Mode 4, terminal cells:
  after_recon_xyb = 0.98 R (huge — patches not yet applied),
  after_patches = 0.026-0.053 R (patches subtract most divergence).
  → patches contribute a separate ~0.03 R residual on screenshots,
    distinct from the EPF residual on photos.

Root cause:
  butteraugli_loop.rs:791 — `let sharpness = vec![4u8; num_blocks];`
  The buttloop uses uniform sharpness=4 for ALL blocks across ALL
  iterations. The production path runs `compute_epf_sharpness`
  AFTER the buttloop and encodes the per-block sharpness map into
  the bitstream. jxl-rs decodes the bitstream and applies EPF with
  the production sharpness map.

  This is INTENTIONAL libjxl-parity behaviour — libjxl's buttloop
  also uses uniform sharpness=4 (documented in W44-113 audit row in
  docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md). But it IS the source of the W44-111
  R/G linear-RGB residual.

W44-117 candidate fixes:
  (a) Run `compute_epf_sharpness` per buttloop iter (expensive,
      ~10-30% buttloop slowdown; would also need to recompute on
      each iter's recon since sharpness depends on it).
  (b) Seed buttloop with one-shot sharpness compute on iter 0
      (cheaper, near-correct after a few iters).
  (c) Accept the gap and keep the qac-scale palliative chain
      (W44-105/107/108/109) as the production solution.

Status quo (c) was implicitly chosen by W44-105's ship. Per
W44-113 the divergence is documented as INTENTIONAL libjxl-parity.
W44-116 confirms the mechanism. Fix decision deferred to W44-117.

Counter-finding: terminal cells have a SEPARATE ~0.03 R residual
that survives gab+EPF disabled (after_patches=0.026 R). This is
distinct from the EPF mechanism and points at patches as a
secondary divergence source. Sub-investigation candidate for
W44-117 phase 2 (after EPF fix decision).

Acceptance gates: PASS.
  - Per-step dump infra zero-cost when feature off (verified
    via cargo build without __internal_recon_hook).
  - 1281 lib tests still pass.
  - Hash-locks unchanged (no production code path modified).
  - First divergent step identified: apply_epf (uniform sharpness
    vs bitstream's compute_epf_sharpness map).
